Subject: Plan for Cantor M2B Windows Platform Preflight Runtime

& [PlanIdentity] is one isolated activation
  + [runtime_profile] is cantor-windows-platform-preflight-runtime/0.1
  + [authority_required] is valid SJS signature
  + [physical_probe] is opt-in and exact-root only

& [Step01] verify source preservation, prior proofs, host facts, and signature
& [Step02] add one workspace member, exact local dependency edges, and no new registry package
& [Step03] implement safe request validation and explicit non-Windows unsupported dispatch
& [Step04] implement one private Windows module with six documented unsafe blocks
& [Step05] implement pure conversion, reserved-field, disposition, zero-error provenance, and final-form gates
& [Step06] add static exact-call, exact-flag, unsafe-count, and forbidden-surface assertions
& [Step07] run focused default debug and overflow-checked release tests without physical effects
& [Step08] create only the exact ignored fixture and run the ignored probe through the governed runner
& [Step09] preserve request, result, host, executable, source, and dependency evidence
& [Step10] run full workspace debug/release, format, lint, build, docs, and audit
& [Step11] regenerate affected evidence in dependency order
& [Step12] close solution, proof, review, readiness, support, narrative, reentry, and publication

& [StopRule] is strict
  + [stop] on source or dependency drift, new call, write access, invalid ownership, unsafe-count mismatch, zero fabricated OS error, partial evidence, fixture escape, unexpected physical outcome, or failed gate
  + [repair] preserve the fault and reprocess before continuing
